      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It doesnt ignore the lights when you enable the \"World\" Mask - However i'd really like to have an option to also see how the world lighting affects my avatar in the personal mirror, even when the World Mask is turned off.\n\nI don't want to see the entire world behind me, i just want to see my avatar, but in the way it REALLY looks in the world, including lights :D",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-01-01T22:04:57.163Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The personal mirror ignores real-time lights. In worlds which exclusively use real-time lights and lack light probes, this results in avatars appearing abnormally dark in such worlds rendering the personal mirror effectively useless.\n\nPlease add either:\n\n- An option to enable real-time lights in personal mirrors\n\n- Add a single light facing the avatar in the personal mirror when there are no light probes / light probes are black and there are no lights in the world.\n\nLikely affects standalone too, but I've only tested on PC.",
